==English==

===Alternative forms===
* [[counter-intuitive]]

===Etymology===
From {{prefix|en|counter|intuitive}}. Coined by {{w|Noam Chomsky}} in 1955 as “counter-intuitive”.<ref>The ''Oxford English Dictionary'' credits this to a microfilm held at the {{w|Massachusetts Institute of Technology}} entitled ''Logical Stucture of Linguistic Theory''</ref>

===Pronunciation===
